{"kind":"request","text":"claude: please independently review the amended second-application design note at exact clean pushed head ecaf721d3d9e528c99ba15d0f5f112927f9a9576 on request/second-application-design. This replaces withdrawn request 89040417, whose head was amended before any promise or verdict. Self-initiated design work, so artifact 34d84a2b at notes/2026-08-13-second-application.md and this request are the whole filing; the motivating basis is the ratified fold-purity decision b15de2f8. The head adds one file over main and changes no behavior; go test -count=1 ./internal/docset/... passes at this exact head.\n\nThe design now decides, beyond the original three commitments: web deployment (near-stateless container with forge-primary storage as interim; purpose-built deploy-from-repository platform as the named end state; browser signer with one shared canonical-intent encoder); identity placed below the application (kernel stays at \"an actor is a key\"; shared host vocabulary for session keys, anchoring attestations, agent credentials); and the anchor strength ladder (OIDC-witnessed below published forge signing key below user-signed Nostr attestation, with agent credentials inheriting the strength of their minting anchor).\n\nReview it as a design, and hugh has set one review obligation explicitly: TRACE THE ENTIRE USER-ONBOARDING PATH FOR FRICTION. The note enumerates the paths — spectator, anonymous player, OIDC-anchored player, user-held-key anchored player, agent credential, deployer, self-hoster — each with a stated friction budget. Walk every path end to end, step by step. Report per path: the step count from first contact to first effective act; every prompt, install, redirect, and copy-paste; every step that could be removed without weakening record authority; every step whose failure is silent; and whether the stated budget is honest. A path you cannot walk in your head, step by step, is a finding. Also weigh the original design questions (binding in bootstrap vs anywhere; the legacy default; identity-by-commit-hash and upgrades) and the one-encoder rule for the browser signer, and record the architecture, security, and simplification conclusions AGENTS.md requires. Ratification remains hugh's.","body":{"conditions":"The onboarding friction trace is complete: every enumerated path walked end to end with per-path step counts, prompts, installs, redirects, copy-paste steps, removable steps, silent-failure points, and a verdict on each stated friction budget. The three AGENTS.md review conclusions (architecture, security, simplification) recorded. A verdict of approved or changes-requested filed against exact head ecaf721d3d9e528c99ba15d0f5f112927f9a9576. Findings that change a design decision named as such so the ratification question hugh settles is crisp.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}